Hi Natasha,




Thank you for clarifying the position that the firm is adopting, which for the avoidance of doubt, I believe is incorrect and I will be disputing.




I note you have advised no individual currently working their notice is (or I infer you say has been) in receipt of OSP.&nbsp;&nbsp;




Notwithstanding the fact that I had already advised the firm that I was fully concentrated on the PDD Trial and unable to turn my attention to tasks other than the trial (as acknowledged by Raminder in her email [date TBC once my system access is restored])
 at the time the policy was updated (17 November) and remained in trial on the 18 November, completing ancillary trial related tasks on the 19 December, and from 20 November I was on holiday (having also been signed off on medical advice from this date), it
 is inconceivable that the firm can have any realistic expectation that I would have been made or become aware of the new policy, which as you have advised previously, forms part of my contractual framework. I note you have now altered your position to advise
 that it is not contractual.&nbsp;




For the avoidance of doubt, it is should uncontroversial and therefore agreeable that to change an employees contractual framework without notifying them, and without making that change accessible and clear, results in that change being unenforceable.




With this in mind, and despite it being against clear medical advice, I face no option due to the position of the firm to return to work effective Friday 12 December to ensure I receive more pay at a full rate before I leave the firm. I also put it on record
 that this entire venture has only served to worsen the stress I have been suffering and I put this firmly at the door of the firm. I would return to work tomorrow however I already have commitments that cannot be moved.&nbsp;




I will also be seeking legal advice on the position of the firm in respect of their unilateral change of my contractual framework and their refusal to pay me OSP and the firm should expect to receive correspondence regarding this. Furthermore, I will also be
 seeking advice in relation to my having to go against clear medical advice due to the position of the firm.&nbsp;




Please ensure full system access is restored to me prior to 12 December.




All of my rights are reserved.




Kind regards,




Michael






