Hi Michael,

&nbsp;

Thank you for your emails, and I apologise for the delay in my reply. I can confirm the firm’s position regarding OSP as follows:

&nbsp;


Your contract makes it clear that any entitlement to pay during absence is subject to the firm’s sickness policy. That policy is not contractual, and we are not obliged to individually notify employees of its content. Employees
 are expected to review policies, which are made available from time to time on HiBob. The applicable policy, in place prior to your resignation and your current period of sick leave, governs any entitlement to OSP and SSP.
The sickness policy uploaded on 17 November 2025 at 09:59:39 was the first formal iteration of a written sickness policy. No previous written sickness policy was in place.
Condition 7(5) relating to OSP was included in this first iteration. The policy was published to clarify eligibility for occupational sick pay going forward.
The firm confirms that no employee currently working their notice is in receipt of OSP under the terms of the policy.

&nbsp;

In line with this, the firm maintains that you are not eligible for OSP during your notice period and any entitlement is limited to Statutory Sick Pay (SSP).

&nbsp;

Kind regards,

Natasha






























