Dear Michael,

&nbsp;

Thank you for your email and for the welcome back. I appreciate you keeping us informed about your fitness for work, and I have answered your questions below.

&nbsp;

Eligibility for Occupational Sick Pay (OSP)
Clause 13.4 of your employment contract states that company sick pay is provided 
“in accordance with the Company’s Sickness Policy.”&nbsp;The Sickness Policy, therefore, forms part of the contractual framework, and its eligibility criteria apply in full. Under the Policy, employees who have given notice of termination of their employment
 are not eligible for OSP.

&nbsp;

To address your question about consistency, I can confirm that the firm has consistently applied the current policy. Employees in comparable circumstances, i.e., those where notice has been given, receive SSP rather than OSP.

&nbsp;

Return to work and IT access
If you become medically fit to return to work before 15 December, please let me know as soon as possible. In this instance, we would arrange for the IT team to reinstate your system access so that you can resume work and complete the handover required before
 your final day.

&nbsp;

Final pay
Your final pay will include:


SSP for the period of certified sickness absence
Payment for your six days of accrued but untaken annual leave
Any days on which you return to work and perform duties before 15 December, which will be paid at your normal rate.

&nbsp;

Regarding the acting-up allowance, this will be included in your final salary, pro-rated to your last day of employment, as you mentioned below.

&nbsp;

Company equipment
Thank you for confirming that 12 December in the afternoon is suitable for the courier collection; I will arrange this accordingly.

&nbsp;

The temporary withholding of £1,000 is only to ensure the equipment is returned. Provided the courier collects the items on 12 December as arranged, the firm will not withhold the amount due to any delay caused by the courier’s
 delivery timeline.

&nbsp;

TELUS Health
I’m glad to hear that you intend to utilise TELUS Health services, and I encourage you to take full advantage of the support available.

&nbsp;

If you need any more clarification or if your fitness to return changes, please let me know, and we will support you accordingly.

&nbsp;

Kind regards,
Natasha

