p;| www.clydeco.com​My pronouns are: he / him​&nbsp;Follow&nbsp;us&nbsp;on&nbsp;twitter&nbsp;@clydecoemp​​​​&nbsp;From: Raminder Grewal &lt;rgrewal@pogustgoodhead.com&gt; Sent: 17 October 2025 17:29To: Anna Varga &lt;avarga@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Plate Litigation &lt;plate_litigation@pallasllp.com&gt;; Matthew Getz &lt;matthew.getz@pallasllp.com&gt;; James Newton &lt;james.newton@pallasllp.com&gt;; Urquhart, Charles &lt;charles.urquhart@clydeco.com&gt;; Riceman, Sarah &lt;sarah.riceman@clydeco.com&gt;Cc: Alicia Alinia &lt;aalinia@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject: FW: Notice of Resignation&nbsp;See below – a distinct change in tone!&nbsp;​​​​Raminder&nbsp;GrewalGlobal&nbsp;HR&nbsp;Director+44&nbsp;(0)&nbsp;7890&nbsp;043&nbsp;718This email and any attachments are confidential and may also be privileged. If you receive this message in error, please contact the sender immediately, destroy the email and any attachments and do not use, copy, store or disclose this email and any attachments for any purpose. Pogust Goodhead does not accept service of documents by electronic means without express prior agreement.&nbsp;Pogust Goodhead is the trading name of&nbsp;PGMBM Law Ltd, a&nbsp;limited liability company registered in England and Wales (no. 6284764) with its&nbsp;registered office at&nbsp;53-64 Chancery House, Chancery Lane, London WC2A 1QS&nbsp;and authorised and regulated by the Solicitors' Regulation Authority. We use the term ‘partner’ to refer to an employee or consultant of Pogust Goodhead with equivalent standing or qualifications. No&nbsp;reference to a partner should be taken to imply partnership for the purposes of the Partnership Act 1890&nbsp;or Limited Liability Partnerships Act 2000. A list of partners is available on our&nbsp;website.&nbsp;For details about what personal information we collect and why, please see our&nbsp;Privacy Policy.From: Michael Burke &lt;mburke@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Date: Friday, 17 October 2025 at 17:27To: Raminder Grewal &lt;rgrewal@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Cc: Alicia Alinia &lt;aalinia@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;, Howard Morris &lt;hmorris@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;, Joseph Moreno &lt;jmoreno@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject: Re: Notice of ResignationHi Raminder,&nbsp;Thanks for coming back to me on this.&nbsp;&nbsp;I intend on responding to your email in full, however I am due to be in court on Monday, so I will not be able to comply with the requested deadline of 5pm on Monday 20 October 2025. I will respond as soon as I am able to.&nbsp;&nbsp;Thanks again, and I hope you have a nice weekend. I hope Alicia is feeling better as well as I believe she is unwell.&nbsp;Kind regards,&nbsp;Michael&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;​​​​Michael&nbsp;Burke(He/Him)Partner+44&nbsp;(0)&nbsp;7960&nbsp;032&nbsp;34407960&nbsp;032&nbsp;344From:&nbsp;Raminder Grewal &lt;rgrewal@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Sent:&nbsp;Friday, October 17, 2025 3:00 PMTo:&nbsp;Michael Burke &lt;mburke@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Cc:&nbsp;Alicia Alinia &lt;aalinia@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Howard Morris &lt;hmorris@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Joseph Moreno &lt;jmoreno@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Raminder Grewal &lt;rgrewal@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject:&nbsp;Re: Notice of Resignation &nbsp;Dear Michael,&nbsp;Thank you for your email.&nbsp; I have also been provided with your emails to Alicia from today regarding a potential article in The Times, suggestions of criminal conduct and concerns over Gramercy.&nbsp; This email responds to them&nbsp;together.&nbsp;As previously communicated to you, we will not be releasing you from your notice period.&nbsp; Your continued attempts to leave earlier than your contract allows are proving disruptive to our efforts to safeguard good governance within the firm.&nbsp;&nbsp;In addition, your conduct threatens to seriously damage morale and be more disruptive than helpful, taking account of the best interests of our clients.&nbsp;We are, therefore, minded to&nbsp;give you the option of being placed&nbsp;on&nbsp;paid leave for the remainder of your notice period.&nbsp; We would view that as regrettable since we are in the midst of the PDD Trial and would much prefer to have you remain&nbsp;working&nbsp;on the team.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;We therefore give you the choice of either to (i) stay working throughout the remainder of your notice period or (ii) go on&nbsp;paid&nbsp;leave effective immediately.&nbsp;If you continue to try to exit early,&nbsp;given the unparticularised nature of your allegations, we can only conclude that you are grasping for reasons to engineer such an exit for your own reasons, which is unprofessional, threatens breaches of your employment contract, and is not in the best interests of our clients.&nbsp; We put you on notice that we will not hesitate to take legal action against you to enforce your employment contract (in particular your notice period and all covenants), nor will we hesitate to take action against any firm that might seek to employ you ahead of your notice period expiring or in breach of your covenants.&nbsp;If you choose to remain&nbsp;working&nbsp;at the firm, we must insist that you focus solely on your work and only raise any further concerns with sufficient particularity and justification so that we can understand them fully and investigate them if necessary.&nbsp; Unclear and unparticularised allegations as you have been raising for the past several weeks are simply improper and must stop.&nbsp;Regarding the specific points raised in your emails:&nbsp;We are looking into your concerns over Gramercy’s recent input into the Litigation Management Agreement and Agency Agreements. &nbsp;Your email was lengthy, so we need time to fully digest your concerns, but we intend to respond early next week.&nbsp; For the avoidance of doubt, the remainder of this email was prepared before we received your email regarding Gramercy.Your suggestion that you cannot act in the best interests of our clients under supervision from other staff is not understood.&nbsp; If you continue to believe this is the case, please explain which members of staff and why, by precise reference to specific provisions of your contract or the SRA Code of Conduct, say this is so.You refer vaguely to potential criminal conduct.&nbsp; This is obviously a very serious allegation.&nbsp; Please now state clearly and unequivocally what precise conduct you are referring to and by which specific people so that we can investigate immediately.As you are aware, the firm has already taken robust action against Tom Goodhead.&nbsp; We take our obligations to our stakeholders extremely seriously and there is not, therefore, any basis for you to seek to exit early.&nbsp; Even if there has been improper behaviour at the Firm – and rest assured, we will investigate any such allegations seriously – that does not give you any justification, under either your contract or your regulatory obligations. Conjecture about what may or may not be published in The Times&nbsp;does not change that position.I look forward to hearing back from you regarding whether you wish to continue working on the case&nbsp;at PG&nbsp;or go onto&nbsp;paid&nbsp;leave by return and in any event by 5pm on Monday 20 October 2025. We remain hopeful that you will agree to continue to work&nbsp;at PG&nbsp;throughout the PDD Trial.&nbsp;In the meantime, and given your reference to protected disclosures and your suggestion that you will cease working on Monday despite the terms of your contract, please confirm that you have and will continue to preserve all documents that might be relevant to your employment with PG and associated covenants.&nbsp;All of the firm’s rights are fully reserved.&nbsp;Kind regards,Raminder&nbsp;&nbsp;​​​​Raminder&nbsp;GrewalGlobal&nbsp;HR&nbsp;Director+44&nbsp;(0)&nbsp;7890&nbsp;043&nbsp;718From: Michael Burke &lt;mburke@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Date: Friday, 17 October 2025 at 09:34To: Raminder Grewal &lt;rgrewal@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Cc: Alicia Alinia &lt;aalinia@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;, Howard Morris &lt;hmorris@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;, Joseph Moreno &lt;jmoreno@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject: Re: Notice of ResignationHi Raminder,&nbsp;Just following up on the below.&nbsp;We have now reached the 17 October - my requested leave date (having already requested to be released prior to this date).&nbsp;Since my last email, further material developments have occurred meaning I must insist I am permitted to leave as soon as possible. Not only do these developments give me immediate concerns regarding Gramercy's continued direct involvement in the managing and supervision of the NOx Litigation, these developments also are intentionally preventing me in acting in what I believe to be in my clients best interests. Furthermore, they also risk causing significant damage to my professional reputation:&nbsp;email chains which confirm Gramercy, as recently as September, were directly involved in the NOX Litigation and they have been giving direct input into Litigations Management Agreements and Agency Agreements. Yesterday, Anna Varga instructed a member of staff to engage with the company retained by Gramercy to give direct input into these documents - despite assurances given to me and the staff directly by the Board and Anna that Gramercy are not involved in the Litigation;I am unable to continue to fulfil the role of acting in my clients best interests under the instruction of other members of staff;the prospect of criminal proceedings being levied against staff within the firm who are now involved in the NOx Litigation; andthe impending release of a Times article regarding 'misuse of litigation funds, a generally toxic culture, and allowing bullying sexism and sexual harassment with specific instances of senior male staff.'&nbsp;I am afraid I am unable to continue to act in my role at Pogust Goodhead. Please confirm by return that I will be permitted to leave my role effective immediately. I am due to travel to London on Sunday night which I will do to empty the flat and I will then attend the office on Monday to return my laptop.&nbsp;&nbsp;I look forward to hearing from you. All of my rights are reserved.&nbsp;&nbsp;Regards,&nbsp;Michael​​​​Michael&nbsp;Burke(He/Him)Partner+44&nbsp;(0)&nbsp;7960&nbsp;032&nbsp;34407960&nbsp;032&nbsp;344From:&nbsp;Raminder Grewal &lt;rgrewal@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Sent:&nbsp;29 September 2025 10:04 AMTo:&nbsp;Michael Burke &lt;mburke@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Cc:&nbsp;Alicia Alinia &lt;aalinia@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Howard Morris &lt;hmorris@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Joseph Moreno &lt;jmoreno@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject:&nbsp;Re: Notice of Resignation&nbsp;Hi Michael&nbsp;&nbsp;Thank you for your note. I’ll review the content today and come back to you soon as I can with a response.&nbsp;&nbsp;In the meantime, please do not take any action with regards to flights or any other matters outlined in your email, without seeking further approval. Thank you.&nbsp;&nbsp;Regards&nbsp;Raminder&nbsp;&nbsp;Sent from Outlook for iOS​​​​Raminder&nbsp;GrewalGlobal&nbsp;HR&nbsp;Director+44&nbsp;(0)&nbsp;7890&nbsp;043&nbsp;718From:&nbsp;Michael Burke &lt;mburke@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Sent:&nbsp;Monday, September 29, 2025 9:53:23 AMTo:&nbsp;Raminder Grewal &lt;rgrewal@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Cc:&nbsp;Alicia Alinia &lt;aalinia@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Howard Morris &lt;hmorris@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Joseph Moreno &lt;jmoreno@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject:&nbsp;Re: Notice of Resignation&nbsp;Dear Raminder,Thank you&nbsp;for coming back to me and for accepting my resignation. My apologies for the delay in coming back to you, as I’m sure you are aware there are a lot of things in the air!Noting your comments regarding my resignation being premature, I disagree with that assessment, but we are where we are. What is important is that we find a way to move forward that ensures the clients of Pogust Goodhead (and other firms) are not prejudiced or detrimentally impacted moving forward and that we are all content with. I trust that my conduct since submitting my notice demonstrates that I am committed to working with the firm to progress this in a professional and orderly fashion. This email has some detail in it so if it is easier for us to hop on a call to try and cut through bits of it or to have a quicker conversation, I'm more than happy to do so.&nbsp;This email is in two parts: i) to address my notice period and when may be a good time for me to depart the firm; and ii) to address on-going travel and litigation needs with a view to finding a pragmatic way to handle future travel etc.Notice PeriodI agree that we need to work collaboratively to find an appropriate point for me to leave the firm, both to ensure the clients are protected and not disadvantaged, and to ensure that I am protected and not prejudiced. My current leave date is I understand the 15 December 2025. There are various important deadlines between now and then an to add a little more colour to those deadlines, the deadlines we have approaching (demarcated as PDD or Quantum) are as follows:06.10.2025 – PTR 2 (PDD)10.10.2025 – receipt of disclosure from Defendants (Quantum)13.10.2025 – Trial starts (PDD)21.11.2025 – Individual Particulars of Quantum to be filed and served (Quantum)11.12.2025 – receipt of disclosure from Defendants (Quantum)19.12.2025 – Trial ends (PDD)19.12.2025 – Applications for January 2026 CMC (Quantum)As is evident, the litigation has a large number of critical deadlines looming. Overlayed with this, is the added complication of each OEM having its own CRO, as well as an overall Pan-NOx CRO.Each individual must apply to the Defendants (individually per CRO and to all Defendants for the Pan-Lead CRO) for permission to be entered into that CRO. This takes up to 5 working days. There is also a process for applying to be removed from each CRO which can, in itself, take some days.Given the level of confidential information in the NOx litigations, someone who is not in one, or all, of the CROs, is necessarily extremely limited as to what they can see, do and work on. For example, they could not actively participate in the trial, nor could they provide any type of meaningful input into any of the directions that fall across the period that they are not in the CRO i.e. the IPQs. If therefore I am held to work my notice until 15 December, I&nbsp;will be unable to attend trial for the final week before Christmas, nor will I will be able to really assist with any work on quantum disclosure, or work on the applications / witness statements for the January 2026 CMC.Considering this, we (both me and Pogust Goodhead) need&nbsp;to realistically consider when my departure should fall, as it should come at a time that will be at the least detriment of the claimants.To that end, it seems sensible, and would be in everyone’s interests, for me to depart Pogust Goodhead on a date that will allow me to start my new role and be re-entered into the various CROs, which does not conflict with any of those deadlines, nor run over a critical part of the trial that I am intended to participate in. To require me to serve my notice such that I leave the firm on a date which conflicts with a major deadline would be of significant detriment to the clients, not only of this firm, but to other firms as well.Having considered the timetable and what is genuinely in the best interests of everyone, especially the clients, it would appear the best date for me to depart Pogust Goodhead is the 17 October. This date falls after the opening submissions, and across the Normal Driving Conditions expert evidence (which is plainly of importance, but falls at the lower end of the scale of importance considering the other critical tasks over the trial period). Exiting Pogust Goodhead then, will allow me sufficient time to commence my new role before substantive evidence relating to the manufacturers starts.Any other date past this, will cause significant issues with my involvement over key aspects of the trial and, I believe, will have a negative impact on the claimants. For a Partner with current conduct of an ALGLO, who has detailed knowledge of all of the cases across the Pan-NOx Litigation, to be unable to participate in the trial, is not in anyone’s interests. The obvious link is that any prohibition on me being able to work on these cases, also directly impacts the Pogust Goodhead claimants and the prospects of their claims being successfully concluded.Without wishing this to become a confrontational or protracted process (as I am committed to progressing this in a professional and orderly fashion), if Pogust Goodhead wish me to remain in post past this date, I would ask that they provide good reason why, including an explanation of why they do not believe this will impact the clients (including why they believe it is in the clients best interests) including the trial timetable and the quantum deadlines.I would ask this be provided to assist me with any future queries that may be raised of me in respect of compliance with my professional and regulatory obligations i.e. &quot;why did you leave during the PDD Trial or&nbsp; why didn't you leave at a point when you would be restricted from working on critical quantum workstreams?&quot;.Future TravelWhile we resolve the issue of my notice period, I am conscious that it is “business as usual” and I am committed to this. As such, I will be needing to continue to travel to London for work in the office and for attendance at trial (while I am still employed by the firm).I appreciate the arrangement I have with the firm is that they will book my flights for me. Given I wish to make bookings into the future, past the date which I have given above as my preferred leave date, I would suggest that it is more pragmatic, to ensure they the firm is not put to more expense than is needed, for me to take charge of booking my flights, which I can then claim back through expenses. Going forward then, flights which occur over the&nbsp;dates of my employment, I would seek to recover in expenses. For any flights booked that occur past my leave date, I would then cover the cost of myself (as I would no longer be in the employ of the firm).This strikes me as inherently more sensible than continuing&nbsp;to have the firm book my flights, as in an instance where the firm has booked a flight for me which is due to take off after my leave date, I would not be able to travel on that flight, and I would need to re-book the flight most likely at a higher price.Additional to this (and at a higher cost), is the flat that the firm has rented for me the duration of the trial. This rental starts on 6 October and runs until 21 December. I am intending on using this for as long as I am with the firm. The firm however, especially if they are agreeable to my suggested leave date, may wish to consider cancelling this booking and instead booking me into hotels until my leave date. This may be something that the firm considered a more pragmatic and financially sound option. I am comfortable either way and am happy to have an open dialogue on how best to manage this.Until hearing otherwise, I will change my flight booking system such that I will make flight bookings personally and the recover the cost via expenses, and I will proceed as if to stay in that flat over the remainder of my employment.I look forward to hearing from you, and should you require anything further, please let me know.Best,Michael&nbsp;​​​​Michael&nbsp;Burke(He/Him)Partner+44&nbsp;(0)&nbsp;7960&nbsp;032&nbsp;34407960&nbsp;032&nbsp;344From:&nbsp;Raminder Grewal &lt;rgrewal@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Sent:&nbsp;18 September 2025 1:52 PMTo:&nbsp;Michael Burke &lt;mburke@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Cc:&nbsp;Alicia Alinia &lt;aalinia@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Howard Morris &lt;hmorris@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Joseph Moreno &lt;jmoreno@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject:&nbsp;FW: Notice of Resignation&nbsp;Dear Michael,&nbsp;I write further to my previous email, to which I have not received a reply. For the avoidance of doubt, your contractual obligations remain in full force and effect, including your duty to serve your full notice period.&nbsp;If you have any questions, please let me know.&nbsp;RegardsRaminder&nbsp;​​​​Raminder&nbsp;GrewalGlobal&nbsp;HR&nbsp;Director+44&nbsp;(0)&nbsp;7890&nbsp;043&nbsp;718From:&nbsp;Raminder Grewal &lt;rgrewal@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Sent:&nbsp;15 September 2025 17:16To:&nbsp;Michael Burke &lt;mburke@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Cc:&nbsp;Alicia Alinia &lt;aalinia@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Howard Morris &lt;hmorris@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Joseph Moreno &lt;jmoreno@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject:&nbsp;Notice of Resignation&nbsp;Dear Michael,&nbsp;I write further to your resignation email received today.&nbsp;It’s disappointing to note that you have chosen to resign, given that the Board have listened to concerns which have been raised and has engaged in a process to allay them.&nbsp; We also note the concerns you raise related to the previous leadership of the firm. The new Board is determined to bring the highest standards of propriety and integrity to the organisation and is confident that the process being undertaken will arrive at a place that will be in the best interests of the Firm, its employees and, most importantly, its clients. Given the above process, your resignation seems premature. As a result, it is with regret, we accept it.&nbsp;The Firm notes your request for an early release and your acceptance of your obligations at clause 16 of your resignation letter. Given the deadlines involved in the case you referred to, at this stage, the Firm would like you to continue working your notice to ensure that the clients are not put at a disadvantage as a result of your decision. To the same end, and at an appropriate point, we would like you to undertake an orderly handover of your files. At that point, the Firm would be happy to discuss an appropriate way forward with you. Please continue working normally in the meantime.&nbsp;Please note that the entirety of your contract of employment remains in place during your notice period. This includes the express obligations set out under clauses 4.2, 16, 17 and 21&nbsp;of the employment contract executed by you with a commencement date of 1st September 2022. Your contract also contains implicit contractual obligations as to “good faith and fidelity”.&nbsp; This includes an obligation to act honestly in all dealings with your employer, not working (or conspiring) with a competitor, not disclosing our confidential information or trade secrets, not actively disrupting the business or enticing colleagues or clients to leave.&nbsp; To this end, it is notable that a number of your colleagues have chosen to resign contemporaneously.&nbsp; Please be aware that the company will not hesitate to take robust action to enforce any breach of your obligations up to and including court action if that becomes necessary. I also bring your attention more generally to the fact that the restrictive covenants at clause 21 of your employment contract, which were varied by your agreement on 14th September 2023, continue to remain in effect for up to 6 months after your effective date of termination.&nbsp;If you should have any questions, please do not hesitate to contact me.&nbsp;Regards,Raminder&nbsp;​​​​Raminder&nbsp;GrewalGlobal&nbsp;HR&nbsp;Director+44&nbsp;(0)&nbsp;7890&nbsp;043&nbsp;718From:&nbsp;Michael Burke &lt;mburke@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Sent:&nbsp;Monday, September 15, 2025 10:24To:&nbsp;Alicia Alinia &lt;aalinia@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Howard Morris &lt;hmorris@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Joseph Moreno &lt;jmoreno@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Cc:&nbsp;HR Team &lt;hr@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject:&nbsp;Notice of Resignation&nbsp;Dear Board and HR,&nbsp;Please see attached my notice of resignation.&nbsp;Kind regards,&nbsp;Michael​​​​Michael&nbsp;Burke(He/Him)Partner+44&nbsp;(0)&nbsp;7960&nbsp;032&nbsp;34407960&nbsp;032&nbsp;344&nbsp;_____________________________________________________ If our account details change, we will notify these to you by letter, telephone or face-to-face and never by email. Clyde &amp; Co’s privacy notice can be found here Privacy notice: Clyde &amp; Co (clydeco.com) Please could we request that all correspondence with us is sent electronically where possible. For matters subject to the jurisdiction of England &amp; Wales and where you have agreed with the lawyer with the conduct of the case that email service is appropriate, please use this address service@clydeco.com for service, subject to the restrictions set out here . Please copy your email to the lawyer with conduct of the case and include our Clyde &amp; Co reference. This email is sent for and on behalf of Clyde &amp; Co LLP, a limited liability partnership registered in England and Wales under number OC326539 and with its registered office at The St Botolph Building, 138 Houndsditch, London, EC3A 7AR, United Kingdom (Tel: +44 20 7876 5000. Fax: +44 20 7876 5111). Clyde &amp; Co LLP is authorised and regulated by the Solicitors Regulation Authority under number 460690 and uses the word &quot;partner&quot; to refer to a member of the LLP, or an employee or consultant with equivalent standing and qualifications. A list of members is available at: www.clydeco.com. This email and any attachments are confidential and may also be privileged. If you have received this message in error, please notify the sender immediately, destroy this email and any attachments, and do not use, copy, store and/or disclose to any person this email and any attachments. "}

