adson remains the lead partner on quantum workstreams, and Matthew Newbould is the Case Lead and partner for three non-Lead Cases (Hyundai, Toyota and Mazda). In the case of Mercedes, where Mr Gallagher was previously the Case Lead, Ms Varga and I have overall conduct on the same basis as described generally at paragraph 37.3. &nbsp;I agree with Carolina that it may not be helpful to add any further detail on financing availability if it means disclosing lender-heavy CPs to drawdown. &nbsp;Nick&nbsp;Nick&nbsp;Turvey​​​​PartnerT:&nbsp;+44&nbsp;20&nbsp;4574&nbsp;1069|M:&nbsp;+44&nbsp;73&nbsp;5503&nbsp;5143E:&nbsp;&nbsp;nick.turvey@pallasllp.com110&nbsp;Bishopsgate,&nbsp;London,&nbsp;EC2N&nbsp;4AYpallasllp.com&nbsp;|&nbsp;LinkedInFrom: Anna Varga &lt;avarga@pogustgoodhead.com&gt; Sent: 30 September 2025 14:56To: Matthew Getz &lt;Matthew.Getz@pallasllp.com&gt;; Tom Crow &lt;tcrow@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Plate Litigation &lt;plate_litigation@pallasllp.com&gt;; Alicia Alinia &lt;aalinia@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Carolina Koschdoski de Souza &lt;csouza@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Helena Yearwood &lt;hyearwood@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Cc: Jessica Fechner &lt;jfechner@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject: Re: Pan-NOx Emissions Group Litigation&nbsp;I am keen to say more if we can.&nbsp;&nbsp;Had a couple of comments from the case leads about the section that mentions them. One is fair and should be reflected in the draft. Could I please ask Pallas to tinker with the wording? At [37.4] we say &quot;each of the lead cases has a case lead&quot; but (a) this includes Merc and Pete was lead of that - I am now, (b) Priyanka is leading on quantum not the lead cases. So the drafting is not entirely precise. Also I am reminded that Matthew Newbould - case lead and partner on Hyundai, Toyota and Mazda hasnt resinged - worth adding a factual statement about this since JLG have the other cases in their sights.&nbsp;​​​​Anna&nbsp;VargaPartner+44&nbsp;(0)&nbsp;7890&nbsp;043&nbsp;699This email and any att