aching our confi requirements with Gramercy, we maybe should&nbsp;Matthew&nbsp;Getz​​​​PartnerT:&nbsp;+44&nbsp;20&nbsp;4574&nbsp;1006|M:&nbsp;+44&nbsp;79&nbsp;8538&nbsp;1095E:&nbsp;&nbsp;matthew.getz@pallasllp.com110&nbsp;Bishopsgate,&nbsp;London,&nbsp;EC2N&nbsp;4AYpallasllp.com&nbsp;|&nbsp;LinkedInFrom: Anna Varga &lt;avarga@pogustgoodhead.com&gt; Sent: 30 September 2025 14:12To: Matthew Getz &lt;Matthew.Getz@pallasllp.com&gt;; Tom Crow &lt;tcrow@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Plate Litigation &lt;plate_litigation@pallasllp.com&gt;; Alicia Alinia &lt;aalinia@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Carolina Koschdoski de Souza &lt;csouza@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Helena Yearwood &lt;hyearwood@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Cc: Jessica Fechner &lt;jfechner@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject: Re: Pan-NOx Emissions Group Litigation&nbsp;Thanks, Matt. I was flagging for completeness but I dont see an immediate need to respond (or indeed ever to these points).&nbsp;&nbsp;Two further points from counsel on @Alicia Alinia&nbsp;witness statement:&nbsp;As to [37.1], is it possible to provide more detail about the September tranche of $30m? Specifically, is the money held and controlled by PG or held by Gramercy for PG to draw down on, and is Gramercy contractually obliged to pay PG on request? Further, when you say “the September Tranche can, contractually, only be used for the NOx Group Litigations” is this a reference to a contract between Gramercy and Pogust Goodhead? If those details are not given, the counsel team thinks Cleary G are very likely to ‘zero in’ on this point. @Tom Crow&nbsp;@Carolina Koschdoski de Souza&nbsp;@Helena Yearwood&nbsp;pls could you consider this point and what we can say? I am minded to agree with counsel that this will be an area of focus and would like to head it off as much as possible. We are looking to file asap so grateful for comments.&nbsp;As to [37.5] and [43], have the case leads who are working their notice periods agreed that they will work under Leigh Day’s direction? D