osts relating to ADR and Expert reports which we are estimating based on Claimant offers made to the defendant during the cost budgeting process. We have discussed the position internally and with costs counsel, and are seeking a level of cover that ensures the clients have sufficient adverse costs insurance in place to provide cover through to a decision on PDD at 60% incurred costs and 100% approved costs. This should effectively provide sufficient cover to see the claimants to the end of the Litigation.&nbsp;I will get back to you tomorrow on the court deadlines as there are a few coming up around this issue. We are also under pressure from the defendants to be able to demonstrate sufficient cover to the end of the litigation.&nbsp;Do you have an indication as to whether there will be capacity in the open markup for the balance of the topup required (the portion not covered by Gemini)?&nbsp;&nbsp;Jonathan, would it be possible to jump on a quick call to update in the afternoon tomorrow?&nbsp;Regards&nbsp;Tom​​​​Tom&nbsp;CrowGroup&nbsp;Financial&nbsp;Controller+44&nbsp;(0)&nbsp;7890&nbsp;043&nbsp;708From:&nbsp;James Burke &lt;james.burke2@wtwco.com&gt;Sent:&nbsp;Tuesday, October 21, 2025 6:31 pmTo:&nbsp;Tom Crow &lt;tcrow@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Cc:&nbsp;Donatas Juskauskas &lt;djuskauskas@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Sarah Bingham &lt;sbingham@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Anna Varga &lt;avarga@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Helena Yearwood &lt;hyearwood@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Jonathan Simon &lt;Jonathan.Simon@wtwco.com&gt;Subject:&nbsp;RE: Enquiry for Additional ATE Cover – Pan-NOx Emissions Litigation&nbsp;CAUTION: This email originated from outside of the organization. Do not click links or open attachments unless you recognize the sender and know the content is safe.&nbsp;Hi Tom,&nbsp;Thanks for your emails on this and apologies for not getting back to you on this until now – I have been in and out of meetings all day.&nbsp;One of these meetings was to discuss the applicability 