uite so black and white, and it would be helpful to get a view from the PG/LD legal teams on that before you finalise the Note.I take your point on the PTR being likely to be incurred by end of July. Likewise, I agree that there may well be elements of Trial Prep approved costs (e.g. brief fees, trial bundles, initial solicitor work) incurred before the end of July, even if the trial is ultimately vacated.&nbsp;I'm away for the rest of the week, but aside from ironing out point 1 above, the note is otherwise good to go.Thanks again,Sarah&nbsp;​​​​Sarah&nbsp;BinghamLegal&nbsp;Director+44&nbsp;(0)&nbsp;7484&nbsp;085&nbsp;187From:&nbsp;Simon Teasdale &lt;S.Teasdale@4newsquare.com&gt;Sent:&nbsp;Monday, October 06, 2025 11:18To:&nbsp;Sarah Bingham &lt;sbingham@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Sophia Thomson &lt;sthomson@leighday.co.uk&gt;; Fiona Huddleston &lt;FHuddleston@leighday.co.uk&gt;; Anna Varga &lt;avarga@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Michael Burke &lt;mburke@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Cc:&nbsp;spopplewell@leighday.co.uk &lt;spopplewell@leighday.co.uk&gt;; Jamie Macfarlane &lt;jmacfarlane@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; KLatham@kingschambers.com &lt;KLatham@kingschambers.com&gt;; T.Barclay@4newsquare.com &lt;T.Barclay@4newsquare.com&gt;; B.Williams@4newsquare.com &lt;B.Williams@4newsquare.com&gt;Subject:&nbsp;RE: Defendants’ Submissions and Draft Order – Costs of CMH2&nbsp;CAUTION: This email originated from outside of the organization. Do not click links or open attachments unless you recognize the sender and know the content is safe.&nbsp;Thanks Sarah, I’ll adjust to take account of that point about % of incurred costs (but will wait for any other comments before doing so).&nbsp;On the Post-July point:We are 100% on the same page for the scenario if Cs win the PDD trial.On scenario B (Cs lose PDD), I think the difference come from these two parts of your list below:Quantum trial will not happen&nbsp;– when we were discussing this earlier in the year pre-PTR, I recall there was hesitation 